    "updated_at": "2026-11-07T06:06:19Z",
    "body": "Patch ready, staged and not committed (worktree agent-abf6cd0a3f6dd9b11). Before: Rotary Offset's centre-cut audit used `plunge_solid::audit_posed`, which treats everything below the stock's top Z over its XY outline as solid. That box also counts the air around the bar. After: `plunge_solid::audit_bar` judges the final posed path against `multiaxis::revolved_bar`. That is the stock (or the part's skin when no stock is set), revolved about the same fitted axis the ladder wraps around. Its radius is the stock's farthest vertex from the axis, never less than the part's, and its length is the span of stations the stock and part cover. A tip counts as in stock when it is closer to the axis than that radius and between the end stations (`plunge_law::Bar`, `first_bar_plunge`, `audit_bar`). The axial cone and the cleared-column test are unchanged. If the bar can't be read, the op is refused by name. Pinned by: center_cut_multiaxis::rotary_offset_is_judged_against_the_true_cylinder (an infeed into the bar is convicted and the tool that isn't centre-cutting ramps; the same descent moved 1 mm outside the radius passes, where the box reading convicted it) and motion::multiaxis::rotary_bar::tests::the_bar_is_the_stock_cylinder_about_the_part_axis. Gates passed: -Tier quick, rotary_verify, rotary_fixtures, golden_cl, center_cut_multiaxis, and clippy with -D warnings. The decision is recorded in RECOMMENDED.md under the M11.3 Owed entry.",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
